# Title: Sampling Schedule Comparison Data Analysis

# Purpose: This script takes the sampling schedules generated by the methods being 
# compared (Pure GA, PCHIP-49 GA, PCHIP-15 GA, PopED, and Tsuchiwata GA all trained 
# on the 10 subset cohorts of 24 patients each) and the static schedules 
# (clinical schedule, best published Tsuchiwata schedule [Tsuchiwata and Tsuji 2023]) 
# and compares performance on the whole 1,000 patient cohort across AUC, Cmax, Tmax, 
# terminal elimination half life (t1/2), apparent clearance (CL/F) and apparent volume 
# of distribution during the terminal phase (Vz/F). Ground truth for error computation 
# was established by running ncappc on the full 49-point profile of all 1,000 patients. 
# Individual percentage error was established via MPE, MAPE, and RMSPE. 
# Statistical comparisons across the methods were conducted at the schedule level 
# with a nonparametric resampling framework. Analysis includes omnibus multi-group 
# comparisons within and across sampling tiers using the nonparametric Friedman 
# rank-sum ANOVA, Exact Sign Flip Permutation Tests, Nonparametric 95% Confidence Intervals, 
# Paired Two-Sided Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Tests, and Paired Permutation Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) Tests.
# All omnibus and pairwise permutation p-values were adjusted using the Holm-Bonferroni 
# step down multiple-testing correction (significant at p<0.05 to control family-wise 
# error rate across simultaneous evaluations of the PK parameters).

# Author: Amirtha Maria  

# Input: simulated_PK_data_1000.csv,all_best_schedules_pure_ga_binary.csv,
# all_best_schedules_pchip_49_binary.csv, all_best_schedules_poped_binary.csv,
# all_best_schedules_pchip_15_binary.csv,all_best_schedules_tsuchiwata_binary.csv

# Output: 01_master_schedule_index.csv, 10_schedule_level_error_summary.csv,
# 21_primary_benchmark_tests.csv, 22_sensitivity1_factorial_swap_tests.csv,
# 23_sensitivity2_pchip15_vs_pchip49_tests.csv, 24_ablation_pure_ga_vs_tsuchiwata_tests.csv, 
# 25_friedman_method_omnibus_tests.csv, 26_friedman_sampling_intensity_omnibus_tests.csv


